venus (Win32 transport): run against a WDDM2 (GpuMmu) viogpu3d KMD (v0.3), as Neptune's transport
does since its WDDM2 support. Under GpuMmu VidMm locks hand out system staging pages, never the BAR,
so a blob's mapping is the KMD's: RES_INFO places a mappable blob in the shared memory BAR, maps it
into the process and has the host map it behind it (UserVa), with no MAP_BLOB packet and no
D3DKMTLock; creates carry a lookup cookie (VIOGPU_CREATE_ALLOCATION_EXCHANGE_EX) that the open,
RES_INFO and RES_RELEASE_WINDOW resolve by, and RES_INFO is retried while the KMD's create is still
queued. The KMD's cookie map is adapter-wide and Neptune's UMD mints pid << 32 | counter from 1 too,
so this ICD's cookies set bit 31 of the counter: with equal values a process that has used D3D11
got Neptune's allocations back for its own (Neptune's ring as the Venus ring) and vkCreateInstance
hung. Commands go to a virtual context (D3DKMTCreateContextVirtual + D3DKMTSubmitCommand, the command in
the DMA packet's private data); a monitored fence, signalled from the GPU and waited for
asynchronously, sets the events the legacy EnqueueCpuEvent signal did. The WDDM 1.3 path and the
D3D UMD (callbacks) path are unchanged. Without this the ring's shared memory never reaches the
host and vkCreateInstance fails (VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY, "failed to allocate/map ring shmem").

